{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" are the kept vertices in the base’s order, at view indices ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view keeps two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and renumbered with one array load per entry and no hashing. A spanning subgraph keeps every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex at its base index.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are, and, if an edge set was given,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when it is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices: an edge’s index is its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rank among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a count per 64-bit word, so the rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"AdjacencyMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices: building"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its edge mask would cost O(m). One on every vertex keeps the base’s rows, edge indices and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The view holds a copy of the base (value semantics), so mutating the original never shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through. Phase 1 needs a base with vertex indices; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with vertex holes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"traps at construction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","title":"SubgraphView","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L27","fileName":"SubgraphView.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph_view"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsSubgraph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubDigraph"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"filtered_graph"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalGraph"},{"type":"text","text":". Kept apart"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"go forward."}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/IndexRow":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IndexRow"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/indexrow","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IndexRow"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","type":"topic","title":"SubgraphView.IndexRow","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A row in index space (successors, predecessors or neighbors): the base’s row with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dropped entries skipped and the rest renumbered. One array load per entry, no hashing. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row holds one reference to the view’s renumbering and edge set (none when the view keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"everything), and walks the base’s position row only under an edge set.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/DirectedGraph-Implementations":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/directedgraph-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"DirectedGraph Implementations"},"doc://GraphOperations/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://GraphOperations/s8CopyableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Copyable"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/UndirectedEdges":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/undirectededges","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedEdges"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedEdges"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The edges of an undirected "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubgraphView"},{"type":"text","text":": the kept edges of the base, in its order, at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its positions."}],"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Base"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"role":"symbol","title":"SubgraphView.UndirectedEdges"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/EdgeIndexRow":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeIndexRow"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/edgeindexrow","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeIndexRow"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"SubgraphView.EdgeIndexRow","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The view’s edge indices of a row of positions: each kept position’s rank, or the base’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own edge-index row when the view keeps every vertex and every edge.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"DirectedGraph","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations":{"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph Implementations","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations"},"doc://GraphOperations/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Graph","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and no type is both. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed"},{"type":"text","text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs."}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/base":{"title":"base","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/base","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"base"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Base"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph the view filters."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/Graph-Implementations":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/graph-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"Graph Implementations"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"SubgraphView","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph_view"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsSubgraph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubDigraph"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"filtered_graph"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},"doc://GraphOperations/s9EscapableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Escapable"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/DirectedEdges":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/directededges","title":"SubgraphView.DirectedEdges","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedEdges"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedEdges"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Base"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"The edges of a directed ","type":"text"},{"code":"SubgraphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the kept edges of the base, in its order, at its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions. Stepping from one to the next skips the dropped ones.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"GraphOperations","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations","abstract":[]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/EdgeRow":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeRow","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/edgerow","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EdgeRow","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","type":"topic","title":"SubgraphView.EdgeRow","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A row of positions (out-, in- or incident edges): the base’s, with the dropped edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skipped. The index row is stepped in step only when the view drops vertices.","type":"text"}]}}}